Title: Someone Like You
Artist: Adele
Key: A major
Tempo: 135
Time: 4/4

# A / C#m / F#m / D, two bars to a chord in the verse and one to a chord in the
# chorus — the harmonic rhythm doubles where the song lifts, which is most of
# what makes the chorus sound like one.
#
# 135 bpm is the recording's own tempo and not a doubled 67: the verse cycle
# measures 14.2 s (bench/inspect_song.py, bar 0 → bar 8), which is eight bars at
# 135.
#
# Note: piano and voice only, arpeggiated, no strummed guitar anywhere. The chord
# engine has the least evidence per frame of anything in this corpus, and the
# third of an arpeggio arrives late — so C#m read as E, and F#m read as F#, are
# the errors to expect here rather than a structural failure.

